course: dictionary
lesson: 744
title: Bathe: one word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: The same word can mean different things in different sentences. Bathe is a good example. Look at the words around it to find out which meaning the writer chose. «Birds bathe to keep their feathers clean» tells you that bathing here means washing in water.
explain: Ask what the word is doing in the sentence. «The room was bathed in sunlight» cannot mean washing in a bath, because a room cannot be washed in sunlight. Here bathed means filled or covered with light. Test your meaning by swapping it in: the room was filled with sunlight, and that still makes sense.
explain: Your clues can come from the rest of the sentence or the whole text. «Sports drinks are sugary and acidic, so sipping them slowly for hours bathes the teeth» tells you the teeth keep being covered by the drink. The word «again and again» gives you the extra clue. When in doubt, check a dictionary.
fact: Bathe is a verb, and it has forms such as bathes, bathed and bathing.
fact: To bathe means to wash yourself or someone else in a bath. In the UK people more often say «have a bath».
fact: To bathe a wound or your eyes means to wash them gently with water.
fact: In the UK, to bathe can mean to swim in the sea, a river or a lake for fun.
fact: To be bathed in light means to be filled or covered with light, as in «bathed in moonlight».
exercise: «Birds bathe to keep their feathers clean and working well.» What does bathe mean here? | To cover something with light | *To wash yourself in water to keep clean | To cry loudly | To hide under a rock
exercise: A nurse says, «Bathe the cut with clean water.» What does bathe mean here? | To dry with a warm towel | To hit something hard | To tie a bandage tightly | *To wash gently with water
exercise: «The room was bathed in sunlight.» What does bathed in light mean? | Painted in dark colours | Locked away in darkness | Washed in a bath of water | *Filled or covered with light
test: «Sports drinks bathe the teeth again and again.» What does bathes the teeth suggest? | Makes the teeth whiter | Stops the teeth from getting wet | *Keeps coating the teeth with sugary acid, again and again | Brushes the teeth clean
test: In the UK, someone says, «Let's bathe in the lake today!» What does bathe mean? | Sit in the sun | Wash in a bath at home | *Swim in the lake for fun | Dust the feathers
exam: «Tigers bathe on hot days» most likely means | Tigers sleep in the shade all day | *Tigers cool off by wading and swimming in water | Tigers hunt only at night | Tigers wash their claws with soap
